  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Syed Mansoor Ahmed Quadri vs The State Of Telangana on 23 November, 2021 Author: Satish Chandra Sharma Bench: Satish Chandra Sharma, A.Rajasheker Reddy The Hon'Ble The Chief Justice Satish Chandra Sharma And The Hon'Ble Sri Justice A. Rajasheker Reddy Writ Petition (Pil) No.295 of 2020 Order:",
    "facts": "The present writ petition is filed by the petitioner, who is a resident of Karnataka, as public interest litigation stating that the police of Telangana are harassing the merchants of Karnataka by registering cases against them. It has been stated that there is no prohibition for selling Tobacco and Tobacco products in the State of Karnataka and as and when persons are arrested in the State of Telangana, the Telangana police, based upon their statement under Section 161 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973, are registering criminal cases against the merchants of Telangana. A reply has been filed in the matter and it has been admitted in the reply that some cases have been registered keeping in view the prohibitory order dated 06.01.2020 issued by the State Government in exercise of powers conferred under Section 30 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and the same is applicable for the State of Telangana. It has been stated that the public interest litigation has been filed by the proxy of accused No.3/Mr. Mohd. Ali, who is accused in respect of Crime No.109 of 2020.",
